Fix follow-up R CI dependency install issue.

Root cause:
- R workflow installed vignette dependencies from cloud.r-project.org, which built source packages on Ubuntu; fs failed, install.packages warned, and rmarkdown remained unavailable until R CMD build failed.

Fix:
- Use the RSPM repository configured by r-lib/actions when available, falling back to CRAN.
- Add explicit requireNamespace checks so missing jsonlite/knitr/rmarkdown fails at dependency installation.
- Extend static workflow policy tests for RSPM and namespace checks.

Validation:
- python3 -m pytest tests/unit/test_r_package_pdf_manual.py tests/unit/test_binding_publication_ci.py -q
- R CMD build bindings/r --no-manual
